Mesa (guest): report virgl context loss through GL robustness

What: when the host offers VIRGL_CAP_V2_RESET_STATUS_BUFFER (OmacVM.app's runtime,
virgl-context-loss-report.patch), each virgl screen (one host context per DRM fd)
allocates a 64-byte guest-memory buffer (VIRGL_BIND_CUSTOM) and every pipe_context
names it with VIRGL_CCMD_SET_RESET_STATUS_BUFFER. The host writes
VIRGL_RESET_STATUS_GUILTY there when it loses the context. virgl then:
  - implements get_device_reset_status (PIPE_GUILTY_CONTEXT_RESET) and
    set_device_reset_callback (called after the next flush, so Mesa switches the
    GL context to its lost dispatch at once);
  - a context that asked for no reset notification (most apps, and ANGLE's own
    context in Chrome) cannot learn about it, so the next flush ends the app with
    abort(), as Mesa's venus does on a fatal ring status. Chrome then restarts its
    GPU process and the page gets webglcontextlost/restored.
    VIRGL_KEEP_LOST_CONTEXT=1 keeps such an app running (drawing nothing);
  - sets device_reset_status_query, so EGL/GLX offer create_context_robustness;
  - st/mesa: KHR_robustness (and EXT_robustness on GLES) also when the driver
    reports resets but has no robust buffer access (Apple's GL 4.1 has no
    ARB_robust_buffer_access_behavior). KHR_robustness allows undefined values for
    out-of-bounds reads; robust buffer access itself stays off, so ANGLE keeps its
    own bounds checks. On virgl/Apple this changes no GL or GLES version;
  - dri: a context asking for robust buffer access (GLX_CONTEXT_ROBUST_ACCESS_BIT_ARB)
    is refused unless the driver has robust_buffer_access_behavior, as EGL already
    does (EGL_BAD_CONFIG/EGL_BAD_MATCH). Without this, offering reset notification
    would hand GLX apps GL_CONTEXT_FLAG_ROBUST_ACCESS_BIT with no bounded reads.
Why: without it a lost host context leaves the app drawing into nothing: Chrome's
WebGL page freezes. With it, robust apps (gl-lost) see GL_GUILTY_CONTEXT_RESET
and recreate their context; Chrome recovers through the GPU process restart.
Applies to: Mesa 26.2.3 (Arch Linux ARM's version on 2026-10-04).
Upstream: upstreamable together with the virglrenderer side; not sent.
Tests: tests/graphics/guest/gl-lost.c (GL_GUILTY_CONTEXT_RESET on the frame the
host lost the context), tests/graphics/context-loss.sh --expect recover --mesa
/opt/omacvm-mesa (Chrome).
